• Create and manage your account, including Google sign-in and invitation codes;

• Buy goods on your behalf, communicate with Sellers, receive, inspect, store and ship your goods;

• Prepare shipping labels and customs declarations, and respond to carriers and customs authorities;

• Process payments, refunds and chargebacks, and prevent fraud;

• Provide customer support and handle claims;

• Keep accounting and tax records required by law;

• Improve and secure our website;

• Send marketing messages — only with your consent; you can unsubscribe at any time.

We do not sell your personal information.

We share only what each party needs:

• Our contracted warehouse, purchasing and logistics partners in mainland China (names available on request) — order details, recipient name, address and phone needed to label and dispatch parcels;

• Sellers and platforms (Taobao, 1688, JD.com, etc.) — we place orders in our own name and warehouse address; we normally do not share your personal details with Sellers;

• Carriers and logistics providers (e.g. Canada Post, DHL, UPS, FedEx and shipping-line operators) and customs authorities (CBSA, China Customs) — recipient details, contents and values;

• Payment processors (PayPal, and AlphaPay if added) — payment information;

• Technology providers — our website hosting provider, email delivery provider, Google (social login), website analytics (if enabled), and backup services;

• Professional advisers and authorities — accountants, lawyers, or where required by law (e.g. court order, CRA).

Our service providers must protect your information and use it only for the services they provide to us.

• Account information: while your account is open and for 24 months after closure, unless you ask us to delete it sooner (subject to the exceptions below);

• Order, payment and shipping records: at least six years after the end of the tax year, as required by Canadian tax law;

• Inspection photos: 12 months after the parcel is delivered;

• Marketing consent records: as long as needed to prove consent under CASL.

We then delete or anonymize the information.

You may:

• ask to access the personal information we hold about you and how it has been used and shared;

• ask us to correct inaccurate information (you can also edit your account);

• withdraw consent to optional uses, and unsubscribe from marketing;

• ask us to close your account and delete information we no longer need to keep;

• complain to us, and if you are not satisfied, to the Office of the Privacy Commissioner of Canada (www.priv.gc.ca).

Send requests to joshuazhou406@gmail.com. We may need to verify your identity. We will respond within 30 days (or tell you if we need an extension as permitted by law). Access is free of charge.

4.1 Our current fees are published on our Fees page. At the date of this version:

• Service fee: 6% of the item price + Chinese domestic shipping, minimum CAD 5 per order;

• International shipping: charged by chargeable weight, which is the greater of actual weight and volumetric weight (L × W × H in cm ÷ 5000 for express couriers such as DHL, UPS and FedEx, or ÷ 6000 for all other lines), rounded up to the next 0.5 kg tier, at the rate of the shipping line you choose;

• Storage: see the Storage & Inspection Policy;

• Value-added services: extra photos, measurements, removal of packaging, reinforcement, insurance, etc., at the prices listed.

4.2 Shipping estimates and adjustments. International shipping quoted before packing is an estimate. After your parcel is packed and weighed, we calculate the actual charge. If the actual charge is lower, we refund the difference to your original payment method (or to your account balance if you prefer) within 5 business days. If it is higher, we will ask you to pay the difference before dispatch; if the increase is more than 10% or more than CAD 10, we will not charge it without your confirmation, and you may instead choose a different line, remove items, or cancel the parcel. We will show you the actual weight and dimensions on request.

4.3 Exchange rate. Item prices in RMB are converted to CAD at the rate shown at checkout, which is the Bank of Canada daily CNY/CAD rate plus a 3% conversion margin. Refunds of RMB amounts are converted at the same rate used when you paid, so you are not affected by exchange-rate movements.

4.4 Sales tax. MyEasyBuy is not currently registered for GST/HST and does not charge GST/HST. If we register, GST/HST will be added to our service fee, storage and value-added service charges as required by law and shown separately on your invoice. Import taxes and duties on the goods are separate (section 7).

4.5 Fee changes. We may change our fees for future orders by updating the Fees page. Changes do not apply to an order or parcel you have already paid for.

You agree not to use MyEasyBuy to:

• buy, ship or import anything illegal in China or Canada, counterfeit or infringing goods, or items listed as prohibited;

• give false information, use someone else’s payment method without permission, or commit fraud;

• resell goods in a way that breaks Canadian law (for example, consumer product safety, labelling or import permit rules) — business users are responsible for their own compliance;

• abuse our staff, interfere with the website, scrape it, or attempt unauthorized access.

• Counterfeit, replica or trademark-/copyright-infringing goods;

• Weapons and replicas: firearms and parts, ammunition, prohibited weapons under Canadian law (e.g. switchblades/automatic knives, butterfly knives, brass knuckles, nunchaku, throwing stars, telescoping batons, pepper/mace spray intended for use on people, stun guns/tasers), and realistic replica firearms;

• Explosives, fireworks, flammable gases and liquids, lighters with fuel, matches, compressed gas cylinders;

• Toxic, corrosive, radioactive or infectious substances;

• Illegal drugs and paraphernalia; cannabis and cannabis products; prescription drugs; unapproved pharmaceuticals; controlled substances;

• Cash, banknotes, coins (as currency), cheques, securities, gift/payment cards, passports and identity documents;

• Live animals, animal or human remains; endangered species products (CITES), ivory;

• Obscene material or material that is illegal in Canada (e.g., hate propaganda, child sexual abuse material);

• Goods subject to Canadian bans or recalls under the Canada Consumer Product Safety Act (e.g. baby walkers, certain small high-powered magnet sets, products with lead or other banned substances);

• Items prohibited by the law of China for export, or by the carrier.

• Lithium batteries and devices containing them (phones, power banks, e-cigarettes/vapes, battery-powered toys); power banks and loose batteries are often refused by air lines;

• Liquids, gels, pastes, creams, perfumes, nail polish, aerosols;

• Powders (including cosmetics and supplements);

• Magnets and magnetic items;

• Food, tea, seeds, plants, soil, wood, meat, dairy, and other products of animal or plant origin (Canadian Food Inspection Agency rules apply);

• Cosmetics, natural health products, medical devices (Health Canada rules apply);

• Radio-transmitting devices (must meet ISED requirements), drones;

• Knives that are not prohibited (e.g. kitchen and utility knives), tools, and sporting goods that could be classed as weapons — only on lines that accept them;

• Tobacco and alcohol (not accepted);

• Fragile items: glass, ceramics, screens — reinforced packing strongly recommended;

• Oversized or heavy items (over the line’s limits).

If we find a restricted item, we will contact you with options (special line, remove the battery or item, return to Seller, or disposal at your cost). Items shipped against these rules are not covered by compensation.

• Prohibited or restricted items shipped without our approval, or undeclared/under-declared/misdescribed goods;

• Seizure, detention, destruction or return by customs or other authorities due to the nature of the goods, missing permits, or your failure to respond or pay duties/taxes;

• Loss or damage caused by an incorrect or incomplete address, refusal of delivery, or failure to collect;

• Defects, quality issues or quantity shortages that existed when the goods arrived from the Seller and were outside the scope of our inspection (we will still help you raise them with the Seller);

• Functional faults of electronics we were not asked to test; inherent qualities of goods (e.g. perishables, melting);

• Delay, except where expressly covered;

• Indirect losses (lost profit, resale or collectible premium, emotional value);

• Goods abandoned under the Storage & Inspection Policy;

• Force majeure events beyond our reasonable control.
